Java evolved from “object-oriented Java with libraries” in Java 8 to a language with concise data modeling, exhaustive type-safe branching, lightweight concurrency, modern native interop, and frequent six-month releases.

The practical upgrade milestones are **8 → 11 → 17 → 21 → 25** (LTS). Java 26 is the latest feature release, not LTS. Java 26 shipped on 17 March 2026. [OpenJDK release history](https://ops.java/releases/) and [JDK 26 feature list](https://www.oracle.com/ca-en/news/announcement/oracle-releases-java-26-2026-03-17/).

